.TH OROC-VERSION 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.4" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-version \- Inspect or bump the project version defined in your configuration file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc version [options]
oroc version <new\-version | release> [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Inspect or bump the project version defined in your configuration file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
explicit oro.toml/oro.ini to update
.TP
\fB\-\-preid=<id>\fR
pre\-release identifier for pre* / prerelease bumps (default: "rc")
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose, \-V\fR
enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
With no arguments, 'version' prints the current semantic version from the [meta] section.
.IP \(bu 2
With a <new\-version> argument, it sets the version to that exact SemVer 2.0.0 value.
.IP \(bu 2
With a release type, it bumps the version using SemVer rules:
.PP
major, minor, patch, premajor, preminor, prepatch, prerelease For pre* / prerelease bumps, '\-\-preid' controls the pre\-release tag (e.g., 'beta').
.IP \(bu 2
The command updates only your app configuration file; it does not call git or create tags.
.IP \(bu 2
oro.toml is the preferred config file, oro.ini is fully supported when oro.toml is absent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc version\fR
print the current project version
.TP
\fBoroc version minor\fR
bump version to the next minor
.TP
\fBoroc version prepatch \-\-preid beta\fR
bump to the next patch and start a 'beta' pre\-release
.TP
\fBoroc version 1.2.3\fR
set the version explicitly to 1.2.3
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
